  "source_notes": "Extracted from mitohealth.com/products/mito-essentials, /mito-core, /mito-ultra, 2026-07-13 -- each page's own full itemized biomarker list used directly (not constructed as additive unions), because Core/Ultra actually swap some of Essential's indirect thyroid assays (T3 Resin Uptake, Free Thyroxine Index, Total T4) for direct Free T3/Free T4 immunoassays rather than simply adding to them -- so Core is NOT a strict superset of Essential's exact marker set, unlike Vitals Vault/Jinfiniti. Prices are current live member prices (member pricing used as canonical, matching how this vendor markets itself -- non-member prices run ~15-30% higher and were not used), which differ somewhat from the pre-migration vendor_tiers DB prices (Essential matched exactly at $89.61; Core drifted from $191.52 to $197.62; Ultra drifted from $1454.73 to $1503.51). Extremely granular CBC/peripheral-smear morphology line items (Acanthocytes, Anisocytosis, Poikilocytosis, etc.) and urinalysis dipstick components are preserved verbatim as raw markers per the data model's fidelity requirement, but essentially none of them will match our tracked biomarkers table (same situation as Goodlabs/Marek's long tail).",
